WEBVTT

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.030
Sorry I'm late.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.700
If you were fighting
General Logi's subordinates,

00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:55.133
then I guess it couldn't be helped.

00:01:57.466 --> 00:02:01.866
By the way... I said I'd prefer
you'd come alone if possible.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.930
It seems you're a popular guy.
Nobody wanted to stay behind.

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:12.596
Oh, bother... Then I'll tell you
what I've found out so far.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:14.903
Okay.

00:02:16.066 --> 00:02:20.966
TOWARDS THE GREAT BLUE SKY

00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:24.296
The woman you're after,
the one who smells like flowers,

00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.703
is named Delphinium.

00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:28.266
And she's a member of
Grankingdom Intelligence.

00:02:28.766 --> 00:02:30.526
The mayor's wife, maro?

00:02:30.633 --> 00:02:34.173
No, a member of intelligence.
In other words, she's a spy.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.330
What's a spy, maro?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.370
A spy conceals their identity,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.600
infiltrates the enemy and
searches for information.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.230
Is it different from
a master informant like you?

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:50.603
We have all sorts of freedom,
but they have no choice but to follow orders.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:53.833
So do you think she is
following Nene's orders?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.830
I'm not sure just yet.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.100
What else do you got?

00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:02.066
After obtaining the Extra Seven
from Jibral Castle,

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.300
she got onboard
a Grankingdom Army air destroyer.

00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:08.796
The name of the ship is the Norg.

00:03:09.066 --> 00:03:10.226
Where did the ship go?

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:12.403
That's unknown...

00:03:12.933 --> 00:03:13.933
What does that mean?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.070
There should be records
left in the Army database.

00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:19.503
Were those records erased?

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.766
That's exactly right.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.730
All the flight data from after Delphinium
boarded with the Extra Seven

00:03:25.766 --> 00:03:28.266
has been erased
from their database.

00:03:28.733 --> 00:03:31.573
It's a run-down old vessel
about to retire.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.170
There are several unclear things
with the other records as well.

00:03:34.966 --> 00:03:37.596
Then let's go to that ship.

00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:41.403
We should board the ship and
check out the records directly, right?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.070
Just a minute, Shu.

00:03:43.233 --> 00:03:45.933
Do you intend to infiltrate
a Grankingdom ship?

00:03:46.266 --> 00:03:49.766
Yeah. That's the only way,
right, Homeron?

00:03:51.266 --> 00:03:53.126
Things aren't that simple.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.430
Are those Grankingdom battleships?!

00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:02.796
Have we been found, maro?!

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:04.533
Don't panic.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.030
They're not Grankingdom.

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.533
They're the battle fleet
from the Sabaru Kingdom.

00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:14.666
They used to be allied
with Grankingdom.

00:04:15.266 --> 00:04:19.796
They have the same type of battleships
because they received military aid.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:20.670
Used to be?

00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:25.826
Sabaru rebelled against Nene's ambition
to rule the world and renounced the alliance.

00:04:26.166 --> 00:04:31.026
And now, Grankingdom has dispatched
a fleet to counter the uprising.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.630
What? Then is this going to
turn into a war?!

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.573
We should get out of here quick then!
Right, Shu?!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.770
If the Grankingdom fleet is
heading this way, that means...

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.800
That's right. The Norg should be
in that fleet somewhere.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.430
Then all the records will be gone
if the Norg is destroyed.

00:04:49.566 --> 00:04:51.626
That means we need to hurry.

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:53.733
Yes. It's not just the Norg data.

00:04:54.233 --> 00:04:59.473
The data concerning Delphinium is
rapidly being erased as well...by someone.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.700
Let's go to that Norg ship,
Homeron.

00:05:03.366 --> 00:05:08.296
Hold it, Shu. I'd like to check out
the Sabaru fleet first.

00:05:08.566 --> 00:05:10.596
We're going to help out Sabaru?

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.370
That's right.

00:05:12.066 --> 00:05:14.596
You know, that could be a good idea.

00:05:27.866 --> 00:05:29.796
Engine Room!
What's happening?!

00:05:29.966 --> 00:05:31.596
We'll crash at this rate.

00:05:31.633 --> 00:05:32.833
Get off my back!

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.403
I'm doing the best I can!

00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:38.333
It's pointless if this is
the best you can do!

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.070
What?!

00:05:41.266 --> 00:05:44.026
It's okay, Deputy Officer.
This isn't anything new.

00:05:44.633 --> 00:05:45.673
But Captain...

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.000
It's okay.

00:05:47.466 --> 00:05:50.966
It was absurd that this Norg was
ordered to this front in the first place.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.600
It's a good chance for us to
distinguish ourselves in battle.

00:05:54.066 --> 00:05:58.226
The Grankingdom Army has
plenty of other battleships.

00:05:58.466 --> 00:06:01.596
They don't expect much from
a run-down ship like this.

00:06:02.266 --> 00:06:04.196
Orders are orders.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.000
Orders, huh?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.930
The fleet headquarters
didn't issue the orders.

00:06:09.266 --> 00:06:13.196
It's the same as that time when
we transported that woman...

00:06:13.533 --> 00:06:15.333
Orders are orders.

00:06:15.766 --> 00:06:17.496
Not again, Deputy Officer.

00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:19.496
What do you mean, Sergeant Major?

00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:24.133
You won't last if you get that pumped up
before we even get to the battlefield.

00:06:24.366 --> 00:06:25.766
Here, have some of this.

00:06:25.966 --> 00:06:26.966
Oh, thanks.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.200
Engine room! Up the power!

00:06:30.766 --> 00:06:33.766
I don't want to go down
in a place like this either!

00:06:35.266 --> 00:06:36.326
Oh, man...

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.630
Take some drinks to
the engine room too.

00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:40.266
That sounds good.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.496
The Sabaru fleet will show up
if we don't get a move on.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.773
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:56.233 --> 00:06:56.903
Actually...

00:06:57.533 --> 00:07:01.503
We would like to be included in
the battle against the Grankingdom Army.

00:07:01.933 --> 00:07:03.273
With those children?

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.133
Don't underestimate us.

00:07:05.166 --> 00:07:06.726
We're Shadow Wielders!

00:07:06.966 --> 00:07:08.966
And defenders of justice, maro!

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.203
Whaâ€”?

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:18.633
We have fought against the Grankingdom
with the power of Shadows.

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:21.303
We want you to give us a ride
in one of your ships.

00:07:21.766 --> 00:07:23.096
Please?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.170
It's okay, right?

00:07:29.466 --> 00:07:30.466
Oh, come on!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.730
That's mean!

00:07:31.766 --> 00:07:33.526
We're powerful, you know!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:44.800
The enemy fleet is presently flying 350 km
to the east by southeast heading northwest.

00:07:45.233 --> 00:07:47.873
Our fleet will confront them head-on.

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:50.896
But was it okay to turn them away?

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:54.003
The likes of Shadow Wielders
are of no use in a fleet battle.

00:07:57.233 --> 00:07:58.833
Well, it's going according to plan.

00:08:04.033 --> 00:08:05.373
Come on, hurry it up.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:06.770
Hey.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.900
Yes, sir?

00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:11.703
I'm going to borrow this ship.
Move out of the way, you guys.

00:08:11.966 --> 00:08:13.026
Yes, sir...

00:08:13.733 --> 00:08:15.533
I thought you just left on a sortie...

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.470
Kluke.

00:08:16.766 --> 00:08:17.766
Leave it to me.

00:08:18.633 --> 00:08:20.173
We'll be borrowing this, maro.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.200
Who're you guys?

00:08:23.533 --> 00:08:24.533
Sorry 'bout that.

00:08:24.566 --> 00:08:25.566
Who're you?

00:08:30.666 --> 00:08:31.326
Hurry.

00:08:33.733 --> 00:08:36.103
I guess this is kind of an assault ship?

00:08:37.066 --> 00:08:38.666
Hey, can you fly this thing?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.930
I'm good at stuff like this.
Didn't you know that, Homeron?

00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:45.296
I didn't get that information.

00:08:45.366 --> 00:08:47.966
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.000
Here we go!

00:09:02.533 --> 00:09:05.173
Air Destroyer Norg, rendezvous
with the Second Torpedo Unit.

00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:07.326
Roger.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.100
The torpedo unit...
means they want us at the front lines?

00:09:11.633 --> 00:09:12.803
We have no choice!

00:09:13.166 --> 00:09:14.166
Hmm...

00:09:14.766 --> 00:09:16.096
Reduce vessel speed.

00:09:16.366 --> 00:09:17.966
R-Reduce vessel speed.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.330
Yes, this is the Norg.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.200
Due to an engine malfunction,
we cannot keep up with the rest of the fleet.

00:09:24.733 --> 00:09:25.403
Whaâ€”?!

00:09:25.433 --> 00:09:27.573
We'll do our best to keep up.
Over.

00:09:28.866 --> 00:09:30.166
What's the meaning of this, Captain?

00:09:30.733 --> 00:09:34.203
It's okay. All crew members!
Get in first battle position!

00:09:34.733 --> 00:09:37.033
G-Get in first battle position!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.070
We will do the best we can
with this vessel.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:39.870
That's all.

00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:40.826
Yes, sir.

00:09:45.866 --> 00:09:46.866
Can we catch up with them?

00:09:47.166 --> 00:09:48.166
Just leave it to me!

00:09:48.566 --> 00:09:51.966
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat-tat.
When is it okay for me to fire, maro?

00:09:52.366 --> 00:09:56.926
Shu, I want to fly like this
on our honeymoon.

00:09:56.966 --> 00:09:58.996
Well, this isn't exactly a vacation.

00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:02.566
Under normal circumstances,

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:07.400
a run-down ship like the Norg
would never be ordered into battle.

00:10:08.066 --> 00:10:11.296
The Grankingdom is building
new ships left and right.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.470
So there must be a reason why
they're going to the trouble

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.270
of sending a ship that's virtually
a pile of scrap to Sabaru?

00:10:17.566 --> 00:10:18.226
Yes.

00:10:18.933 --> 00:10:20.733
You think they're trying to get rid of it?

00:10:21.266 --> 00:10:24.096
I wonder who's trying to hide what?

00:10:24.733 --> 00:10:30.633
It's the work of the one ordering Delphinium.
That person has the Extra Seven.

00:10:30.666 --> 00:10:32.496
That's just a guess, right?

00:10:33.033 --> 00:10:36.673
You know master informants
only discuss facts, right?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:37.770
We're catching up!

00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:49.433
It's the Grankingdom fleet!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.470
What?! They're here already?!

00:11:00.766 --> 00:11:04.426
Leave it to me, maro.
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.300
What're you doing, Marumaro?!

00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:18.533
It's not my fault, maro!

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.530
Hold it, are we going to go into that?

00:11:25.233 --> 00:11:26.503
Let's go, Kluke!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.230
Hey, that's crazy!

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.070
I'm telling you, let's go back.
Please, Shu?

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.170
I'll shoot them all down,
so it'll be okay, maro.

00:11:35.433 --> 00:11:36.103
Here we go!

00:11:36.333 --> 00:11:37.633
What?!

00:11:37.666 --> 00:11:39.696
Heh. Now that's our Kluke.

00:11:40.066 --> 00:11:40.726
Go!

00:12:03.966 --> 00:12:06.226
First Torpedo Unit,
prepare to charge!

00:12:10.433 --> 00:12:11.833
You idiot! Not yet!

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:16.400
That's the unit reported to have
been stolen by Shadow Wielders.

00:12:16.733 --> 00:12:19.373
Those guys, huh?!
What do they intend to do?

00:12:23.366 --> 00:12:24.896
D-Dodge that, Kluke!

00:12:26.433 --> 00:12:28.333
Hey, keep it down, will you?!

00:12:32.666 --> 00:12:34.526
Kluke, get us out of here quick!

00:12:34.566 --> 00:12:37.326
Kluke, missiles.
Fire some missiles or something.

00:12:37.366 --> 00:12:39.396
Hang on a second.
Let me check the manual.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.370
- We're done for!
- Fire the missiles!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.670
Keep quiet!

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.970
What're you doing, Marumaro?!
Hurry up and counterattack!

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:48.573
Leave it to me, maro!

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:54.430
I'll nail them with every shot!
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat!

00:12:54.466 --> 00:12:57.996
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat!

00:13:00.133 --> 00:13:02.133
The gun won't fire, maro!

00:13:02.233 --> 00:13:04.973
It seems the safety circuit activates
if the gun is fired too much

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.770
and the barrels overheat.

00:13:07.266 --> 00:13:08.266
These are the missiles.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.130
Lock on, Kluke.

00:13:10.733 --> 00:13:11.733
I'll give it a shot!

00:13:12.766 --> 00:13:14.126
Firing missiles!

00:13:19.666 --> 00:13:20.666
All right!

00:13:22.166 --> 00:13:24.266
Which ship is the Norg?

00:13:24.633 --> 00:13:28.173
It's a small ship. It has an ID number
written on the body of the ship.

00:13:28.533 --> 00:13:30.733
There are a bunch of small ships.

00:13:32.066 --> 00:13:33.066
Isn't that it over there?!

00:13:33.466 --> 00:13:35.526
It's so far away I can't see the number.

00:13:35.766 --> 00:13:37.596
The Norg is a rickety old ship, right?

00:13:37.833 --> 00:13:40.233
That's the only ship
that's moving along slowly.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.200
Kluke, try approaching it.

00:13:42.433 --> 00:13:43.433
Got it.

00:13:46.033 --> 00:13:47.473
How're you going to get inside?

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.970
I just have to jump over there.

00:13:51.033 --> 00:13:53.373
Homeron, I'll send you over!

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.766
Send me? Don't tell me...

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.570
That's right. With Blue Dragon.

00:14:01.333 --> 00:14:05.473
ID number 214.
No mistake, that's the Norg.

00:14:05.666 --> 00:14:06.796
Here we go!

00:14:08.866 --> 00:14:11.396
There's an enemy ship
approaching from the port side!

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:13.470
Fire anti-aircraft!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:14.900
Fire anti-aircraft!

00:14:18.533 --> 00:14:20.033
Kluke, take us up!

00:14:20.066 --> 00:14:21.066
Roger!

00:14:24.833 --> 00:14:26.033
Here we go, Homeron!

00:14:26.366 --> 00:14:28.426
R-Right. I'm counting on you, Shu.

00:14:29.033 --> 00:14:30.033
Here we go.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:35.670
The Norg's getting away.

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:37.533
Don't let them get away,
Blue Dragon!

00:14:37.966 --> 00:14:39.296
Hold it right there!

00:14:41.866 --> 00:14:43.866
Good work. Here's fine.

00:14:44.166 --> 00:14:45.196
See you around.

00:14:49.666 --> 00:14:50.326
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:14:57.766 --> 00:14:58.766
All right!

00:15:04.233 --> 00:15:05.233
It's a success.

00:15:05.266 --> 00:15:06.526
What do we do now?

00:15:06.933 --> 00:15:08.873
We'll keep a distance from
the Norg and stand by.

00:15:09.366 --> 00:15:11.826
We'll pick Homeron up
once he signals us.

00:15:12.833 --> 00:15:13.503
Got it.

00:15:13.633 --> 00:15:16.633
Maro!
Kluke! Up front, maro!

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:17.370
What?!

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.070
I can't believe that ship earlier
would just charge in solo like that.

00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:44.733
They must've been out of their minds.

00:15:45.066 --> 00:15:46.066
Hmm...

00:15:46.933 --> 00:15:49.333
We might've been targeted.

00:15:49.833 --> 00:15:50.503
No way...

00:16:11.166 --> 00:16:12.296
Have we been hit?!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.530
I can't control it!

00:16:19.833 --> 00:16:24.173
I can't see ahead.
It's totally white up ahead, maro.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.230
You sure picked
a great place to land, maro!

00:16:37.266 --> 00:16:39.466
I didn't land here
because I wanted to!

00:16:43.133 --> 00:16:44.833
What should we do?
It won't move.

00:16:44.966 --> 00:16:47.466
We've got to repair it quickly!
I'm counting on you, Kluke.

00:16:47.833 --> 00:16:48.503
Right.

00:16:48.566 --> 00:16:49.566
I'll help.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:53.570
It's the enemy!

00:16:53.766 --> 00:16:54.766
What?

00:16:54.866 --> 00:16:55.526
Maro!

00:17:08.466 --> 00:17:09.466
Was that a direct hit?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.170
We've been hit on the port side.
Fire has broken out!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.770
Oh my. I guess that's
enough for now.

00:17:18.266 --> 00:17:20.166
We still haven't even
brought down one ship!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.630
It's okay.
Otherwise we'll go down first.

00:17:22.933 --> 00:17:25.333
But now that we've
entered the battlefield...

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:26.830
Get down!

00:17:37.166 --> 00:17:40.366
Deputy Officer, increase our altitude.
We'll crash at this rate...

00:17:58.166 --> 00:18:00.626
No good. This is the best I can do.

00:18:01.033 --> 00:18:03.703
Who're you?! What happened
to the Deputy Officer?

00:18:05.533 --> 00:18:07.473
I made it somehow...

00:18:09.333 --> 00:18:11.033
We're withdrawing from this battle.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.470
I agree with that idea.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:14.770
But who are you?

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.430
My name's Homeron.
I'm a master informant.

00:18:18.833 --> 00:18:21.633
Homeron?
I've heard that name before.

00:18:22.233 --> 00:18:23.233
That's nice to hear.

00:18:23.566 --> 00:18:27.466
What's the world's best master informant
doing on this rusty old ship...

00:18:27.966 --> 00:18:29.866
A ship that's about to go down...

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.030
Are you a Sabaru spy?!

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.400
It seems we don't have much time,
so I'll be brief.

00:18:35.066 --> 00:18:38.496
I'm on the trail of a woman
named Delphinium.

00:18:39.933 --> 00:18:41.073
It seems you know her...

00:18:41.666 --> 00:18:45.496
You let her board this ship
near Jibral Castle, right?

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:49.630
I want to know where you took her.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.030
For some reason,
there's no information about that

00:18:53.066 --> 00:18:55.766
in the army's database or
in this ship's database.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:19:01.230
I don't recall erasing it...
But I have no intention of telling you.

00:19:01.666 --> 00:19:05.926
Well, soon you won't be able to
even if you wanted to.

00:19:06.033 --> 00:19:07.173
What're you getting at?

00:19:07.833 --> 00:19:13.273
Somebody is attempting to conceal where
Delphinium went from Jibral Castle.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:17.070
Now that all the data has been erased,
the only ones who know are...

00:19:17.933 --> 00:19:18.603
That's right...

00:19:19.033 --> 00:19:23.733
Only you guys, the crew of this ship
that actually transported her...

00:19:24.133 --> 00:19:25.133
No...

00:19:25.566 --> 00:19:30.266
Doesn't it seem strange that a decrepit
old ship like the Norg was sent to the front?

00:19:31.366 --> 00:19:34.926
It's true... Just us being here
is a liability for the whole fleet.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:41.170
So you're saying the plan was to have
the Norg participate in this battle

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.000
and have us go down with it?

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.170
Don't talk nonsense!

00:19:45.833 --> 00:19:48.673
We're done, Captain!
This ship won't hold on any longer!

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.100
I guess this is it...

00:19:56.133 --> 00:19:58.903
You're going to help us out.
We're getting off of this ship.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:00.500
Captain...

00:20:00.766 --> 00:20:04.066
It's okay. We're helping each other.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:08.100
If what he's saying is a lie,
we just won't send him back alive.

00:20:09.066 --> 00:20:10.066
Fine with me.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:12.600
It's General Logi.

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:17.470
We sent that woman to General Logi.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:19.870
Captain, that's classified information.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.770
General Logi...

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.200
The general of the Grankingdom
who's after Shu and the others...

00:20:28.966 --> 00:20:31.496
Indeed, with Logi's abilities,

00:20:31.533 --> 00:20:34.573
it's possible to provide
Delphinium with resources.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.770
Then everything makes sense...

00:21:38.733 --> 00:21:40.273
Crushing Nail!

00:21:43.866 --> 00:21:46.166
Let's take out this entire ship, maro!

00:21:46.366 --> 00:21:47.566
Shall we, Marumaro?!

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:50.000
Don't be reckless.
We'll lose our footing.

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.570
Here they come!

00:22:01.766 --> 00:22:06.126
Oh no! A whole bunch more have come.
Kluke, hurry up.

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.870
It's this pipe here!
This is the problem!

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:11.270
It doesn't look like there are
any replacement parts.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.730
I'll patch it up for now.

00:22:13.033 --> 00:22:16.203
I'll close this system and
stop a portion of the engine.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.300
Oh, look!

00:22:22.333 --> 00:22:24.303
Isn't that the ship Homeron boarded?!

00:22:31.366 --> 00:22:32.366
Homeron!

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:37.900
Damn it!

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:22.970
Shu and the others head off
to rescue Homeron,

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.070
but encounter a herd
of savage monsters.

00:24:25.133 --> 00:24:26.803
There's way too many
of them, maro.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:29.270
Shu, let's beg for
our lives together, maro.

00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:31.030
Huh? Okay, got it.

00:24:31.066 --> 00:24:33.396
Here goes, maro.
Life, maro.

00:24:33.433 --> 00:24:36.303
Spelling out a word with your body?!
How do I do it?

00:24:36.466 --> 00:24:39.196
Next on Blue Dragon:
Pursuit of the Devil
